course: dictionary
lesson: 8351
title: Same word, different meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words look the same but have different meanings. The clues are in the words around them. Look for a word that fits: is it a thing, an action, or a colour? «Look at a rose stem covered in tiny green aphids sucking sweet sap.» A stem and sap belong to a plant, so rose means a flower here.
explain: Rose can also be the past form of rise, which means went up. «The sun rose over the hills.» Try swapping in «came up»: the sun came up over the hills, and that still makes sense. So rose is the past form of rise here.
explain: Rose can also be a soft pink colour. «Her cheeks turned rose with the cold» is not about a flower, because a flower cannot turn pink from the cold. Check the sentence again: which meaning fits best? When you are unsure, read the sentence aloud with each meaning and listen for the one that sounds right.
explain: Rose can be a girl's name, too. «In Brisbane, Nanna buys Ava-Rose an ice cream every arvo.» The capital R and the name Ava-Rose tell you this is a person. Capital letters are a clue: a name starts with one, and a flower does not.
fact: Rose has three main meanings: a flower, the past form of rise, and a soft pink colour.
fact: «Rose» means a flower with a sweet smell and sharp thorns on its stem.
fact: «Rose» as the past of rise means went up, as in «The sun rose».
fact: Rose is also a girl's name, often written with a capital letter.
fact: In French, «rose» also means pink, and «une rose» means a rose flower.
exercise: «Look at a rose stem covered in tiny green aphids sucking sweet sap.» What is a rose in this sentence? | A pink colour | A girl's name | The past form of rise | *A flower on a plant
exercise: «The sun rose over the hills this morning.» What does rose mean here? | Grew a flower | Turned pink | *Came up | Shouted
exercise: In «Ava-Rose», what kind of word is Rose? | *A name | The past form of rise | A flower | A colour
test: Nadia wants a bunch of roses for her mum. What are roses? | The past form of rise | A girl's name | *Flowers with thorns on the stem | A soft pink colour
test: «The price of bread rose again this week.» What does rose mean here? | Was cut | Smelled sweet | *Went up | Turned pink
exam: «The dress was rose pink.» What does rose mean here? | A flower with thorns | *A soft pink colour | The past form of rise | A girl's name
